# `/` Top (Screen Requirements)

The requirements of the **minimal page for checking that the app runs**, which stands in place before any screen is built. Once a
screen is being built, replace this whole document with that screen's requirements.

## What It Shows

| Section | Content |
| --- | --- |
| Heading | The name of this site |
| Description | What this site is |

## What Not to Write

**No navigation paths.** This scaffold has no screen to lead to, so placing one would make an action with nothing behind it.

## Layout Shell

**It does not pass through a layout shell.** There is no route group layout shell, so this screen places `main` itself.

## Why This Screen Cannot Be Empty

Where a not-found screen leads back to, where a request lacking a role is sent back to, and the public routes the sitemap lists all
point at this entry point. Emptying it leaves every one of those paths without a destination (what points here is held by the
implementation).

